{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/806414-question-about-learning-gifts-outside-your-tribe-breed-auspice","id":806414,"title":"Question about learning gifts outside your tribe/breed/auspice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T13:31:14-08:00","id":806414,"title":"Question about learning gifts outside your tribe/breed/auspice","content":"I remember reading once that a garou can only learn gifts level 1-3. Rank4-5 and camps were cut off from them. I can't remember where I read this. Does anyone know where it came from or am I confused?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:48:49-08:00","id":806438,"title":"","content":"Garou can pretty much learn every gift there is if a spirit or a person who knows the gift teaches.<br /> If the garou has a special knack for the gift (it is from his breed, auspice or tribe) the experience points are 3XP per rank of the gift, otherwise 5XP per rank.<br /> Learning gift from other Changingbreeds is possibly, but STs should opt to increase the rank by one.<br /> Gifts that require specific anatomy, like wings, can't be learned.<br /> <br /> Learning from a spirit is basically being bestowed with the gift and can take many forms. Learning from garou instructors is more like trail and error and can be nasty if the gift has side-effects like &quot;Silver Claws&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:26:01-08:00","id":806466,"title":"","content":"Keeping Rank 4-5, and Camp, Gifts away from players is - to the best of my knowledge - a house rule common in LARPs and similar large scale games.<br /> <br /> Now, certain Gifts (not just those specific sets, but most of them fall into those) are generally only taught by either spirits or Garou that would not readily teach them to outsiders, but everything has a price. And it in-character it should never be as simple as, &quot;Rat spirits aren't going to teach non-Gnawers/Ratkin high level Gifts.&quot; Various Totem spirits, who's in your pack, and all sorts of factors can weigh in on how willing teachers are to impart their Gifts to others. And of course, there's simply how good your Theurge is, and how good your chiminage is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T11:47:16-08:00","id":807179,"title":"","content":"The Corax book mentioned gift/rite stealing there was a brief explanation on it basically rank 1-3 were open barring a specific condition, i.e. gift requiring a trait a character did not possess. At least a mention was made about learning gifts that had a set level i.e. Bastet stepping sideways before rank 4 unless they were a Swara. <br /> I as a Storyteller tend to restrict players access to Level 4 and 5 gifts unless the players are willing to do a lot of work in game to get access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:06:33-08:00","id":807195,"title":"","content":"Its easier to justify Someone not teaching, a tribal gift in particular, if its high level... then again... a Homid garou who wants to learn &quot;Curse of lycanon&quot; might find a sympathetic red talon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:42:35-08:00","id":807217,"title":"","content":"I tend to frown on players buying gifts out of auspice, know your role as they say....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T13:47:20-08:00","id":807270,"title":"","content":"Considering that plenty of Auspice Gifts are Gifts in other lists, it's really not that hard to justify a lot of them out of Auspice.<br /> <br /> If you're the Ragabash of a War Pack, and often act as a scout/harasser in tactical situations, there's lots of Galliard and Ahroun Gifts that would be appropriate to your Auspice role.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:07:42-08:00","id":807667,"title":"","content":"&quot;Resist Pain&quot; is one of the best rank 1 gifts and kind of a combat oriented gift, yet it is one the Philodox and Child of Gaia lists. While the Ahroun is the warrior amongst warriors, all fostern soak enhancing gifts are tribal gifts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T08:14:23-08:00","id":809590,"title":"","content":"could see Lunas blessing being easily Relevant to an Ahroun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:15:46-08:00","id":810812,"title":"","content":"If a garou is learning gifts outside his auspice to perform a duty they are not supposed to do then you could consider a renown penalty. I always liked the idea of gifts outside the norm to be rewards for plot points. Maybe a rat spirit will teach the pack a gift normally reserved for bone gnawers for helping it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:03:01-08:00","id":813377,"title":"","content":"Back to the question:<br /> It's in the Plsyer's Guide, page 189, but the rules are a little bit different than you mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}